<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <h1>Community rules & privacy</h1>
  <h2>Repair safely, together</h2><p>
    18+ only. Be honest and respectful. No stolen goods, weapons, illegal modifications, safety bypasses, harassment or spam. Meet publicly, preferably at a repair event. Never pay in advance for unseen work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mains voltage, gas, vehicle brakes/steering, swollen batteries, medical devices and lifts need qualified help. Do not attempt hazardous repairs based on comments. Repairs may affect manufacturer warranties. Back up and protect device data first.
  </p>
  <h2>Independent people, no middleman</h2><p>
    werepair.fyi is a directory and community, not the repair service provider. Prices, parts and warranties are agreed directly and documented by the requester. There is no platform payment or insurance.
  </p>
  <h2>Organiser responsibilities</h2><p>
    Confirm venue permission, accessible space, qualified supervision, electrical isolation, fire safety and first aid. Owners stay with devices; no items are left behind. Apprentices work only under supervision.
  </p>
  <h2>Privacy & moderation</h2><p>
    Names, neighbourhoods, skills, request descriptions and reviews are public. Emails and phone numbers are private; phone numbers stay hidden until verification exists. Do not post home addresses, serial numbers, faces or private data in text or photos. Request photos are public but are never automatically copied to Wikimedia Commons or the wiki.
  </p>
  <p>
    Report harmful content using the report links. The organiser may remove content or suspend an account. Appeals, account recovery, deletion and export requests are handled manually at <a href="mailto:hello@werepair.fyi">hello@werepair.fyi</a>. Public wiki edits follow MediaWiki history and licensing. Minimal incident records may be retained as required by law. No ads, trackers or sale of user data.
  </p>
  <p>
    Maps load from OpenStreetMap when viewed. Knowledge is CC BY-SA 4.0; code is AGPL-3.0. This POC uses fictional demo records.
  </p>
</Layouts.app>
